WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.380
Do you use AI every day,

2
00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.460
and it keeps making the same mistake?

3
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.760
You explain again,

4
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.840
correct it again,

5
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.300
and next week it's all the same.

6
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.020
Hi, I'm Nei Maldaner,

7
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.380
and in this video I want to

8
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.540
show you why this happens.

9
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.700
The problem is almost never the model.

10
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.140
It's what surrounds it.

11
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:19.880
Let's talk about

12
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.620
IA Cultivada,

13
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.680
cultivated AI.

14
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.920
It's not a product,

15
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.340
and it's not a new model.

16
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.100
It's a way to build AI systems

17
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.240
whose behavior improves through cycles:

18
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.880
execute, evaluate, give feedback,

19
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.280
adjust, and execute again.

20
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.300
By the end,

21
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.360
you'll know what level the AI you

22
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.000
use today is at.

23
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.400
Think of traditional software as building a

24
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.040
house.

25
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.560
Foundation, walls, roof,

26
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.380
finishing touches.

27
00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:46.740
You define the structure,

28
00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.960
the rules, and the expected result upfront,

29
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.760
and you get exactly what was specified.

30
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.860
When it fails,

31
00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.380
it's a bug on one line.

32
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.880
Now think about a garden.

33
00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.140
You don't draw every leaf.

34
00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.440
You choose the seed,

35
00:00:58.440 --> 00:00:59.680
prepare the soil,

36
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:00.800
provide water and light,

37
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.820
and what grows is the result of

38
00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.220
the conditions you created.

39
00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:05.620
That's how AI works.

40
00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.580
Nobody wrote a model's ability to plan

41
00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.880
or code, line by line.

42
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.380
The labs created the conditions,

43
00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.260
and the ability emerged.

44
00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.760
Before, we programmed behavior.

45
00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:19.680
Now, we program the process that produces

46
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.660
behavior.

47
00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.740
Let's name each part.

48
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.660
The seed is the AI model.

49
00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.700
The soil is the context.

50
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.920
The environment is the system where the

51
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.300
agent works.

52
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.240
Water and light are the examples,

53
00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.620
rules, and tools.

54
00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.240
Pruning means corrections.

55
00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.400
Observation means evaluation.

56
00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.300
Fertilizer is feedback.

57
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.760
And each harvest is a new version

58
00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:42.640
of the agent.

59
00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.320
Now pay attention to the point almost

60
00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:45.760
everyone gets wrong.

61
00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.260
The right idea isn't:

62
00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.140
I plant an AI and wait for

63
00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:49.900
it to grow.

64
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.660
It's: I prepare the environment,

65
00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.820
put the AI to work,

66
00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.240
observe its behavior,

67
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.380
evaluate the result,

68
00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.900
and adjust the system.

69
00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.840
I plant, observe,

70
00:01:58.840 --> 00:01:59.980
evaluate,

71
00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.260
adjust the environment,

72
00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.940
and grow it again.

73
00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.260
Don't take the lazy interpretation.

74
00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.260
IA

75
00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:09.240
Cultivada doesn't mean less structural work.

76
00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.800
It means a different kind of structure.

77
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:12.760
With a house,

78
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.980
almost all the work happens before construction

79
00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:15.960
is finished.

80
00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.140
In a garden,

81
00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.720
an important part happens after the agent

82
00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:20.860
starts operating.

83
00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.760
The cycle goes like this:

84
00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.520
use it, observe,

85
00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.420
record failures, evaluate,

86
00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.740
correct, and only then increase autonomy.

87
00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.480
And there's more:

88
00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.460
a plant grows on its own;

89
00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:34.940
an agent doesn't.

90
00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.780
Without evaluation and feedback,

91
00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:37.980
it

92
00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.680
repeats the same mistake forever,

93
00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.240
with the same confidence.

94
00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.140
It can even deliver a polished result

95
00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:43.900
that's wrong.

96
00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.100
That's

97
00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.760
exactly why evaluation

98
00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:47.640
exists.

99
00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.120
Another important point.

100
00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.420
While you're using it,

101
00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.520
the model usually isn't changing its own

102
00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:53.360
weights.

103
00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:54.740
It arrives ready,

104
00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:55.640
frozen.

105
00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.220
So when someone says the agent got

106
00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.740
better, something else changed.

107
00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.820
The context changed.

108
00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:03.620
The memory.

109
00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.320
The rules.

110
00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.160
The examples.

111
00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.320
The tools, prompts,

112
00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:09.360
skills, architecture,

113
00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.320
processes, and evaluation criteria.

114
00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.440
In other words,

115
00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.540
often what improves isn't the seed.

116
00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.920
It's the garden.

117
00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.240
And that's great news.

118
00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.720
Because the model is the same one

119
00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:20.960
your competitor has.

120
00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.600
The garden isn't.

121
00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.040
The garden is yours,

122
00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.200
and it's made of files you write

123
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.320
and review.

124
00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.160
There are two levels of cultivation,

125
00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.800
and many people mix them up.

126
00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.000
At the first level,

127
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.480
the lab cultivates the model:

128
00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.580
architecture,

129
00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.540
data, objectives,

130
00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.080
computing power, training,

131
00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.200
and feedback.

132
00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.880
This happens at Anthropic,

133
00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.680
OpenAI, and Google.

134
00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.740
It costs billions,

135
00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.200
and you don't take part.

136
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.340
At the second level,

137
00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.700
you cultivate the agent:

138
00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.620
its role, context,

139
00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.520
tools, rules, examples,

140
00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.820
memory, evaluation, and feedback.

141
00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.300
The model arrives ready.

142
00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.280
What you cultivate is the envelope around

143
00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:57.540
it.

144
00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.940
And that envelope is what turns the

145
00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:02.320
same model into either a confused intern

146
00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.620
or a reliable professional.

147
00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.620
Every agent is cultivated using the same

148
00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.040
eight elements.

149
00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:10.400
One: role.

150
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.520
What is it responsible for?

151
00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.700
One clearly defined thing.

152
00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.100
Two: context.

153
00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.020
What does it need to know?

154
00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.050
One good page is worth more than

155
00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.460
twenty dumped on it.

156
00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.900
Three: tools.

157
00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.960
What can it operate?

158
00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:25.960
Four:

159
00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:27.540
rules and limits.

160
00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.900
What does it do on its own,

161
00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.860
what does it ask you to confirm,

162
00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:32.680
and what does it never do?

163
00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.500
These four make the agent work.

164
00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:38.240
The next four make it improve.

165
00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.720
Five: examples.

166
00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.060
Six: memory.

167
00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:42.540
Seven: evaluation.

168
00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.520
Is it good,

169
00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:44.840
compared to what?

170
00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.440
And eight: feedback,

171
00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.780
which turns every failure into a change

172
00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:49.800
in the environment.

173
00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.180
Most people stop at number four and

174
00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:54.269
complain that AI doesn't learn.

175
00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.000
IA Cultivada isn't

176
00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.920
an official product category.

177
00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:00.380
The same Claude,

178
00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.740
Codex, or Gemini can work in a

179
00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:05.140
traditional way or a cultivated way.

180
00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.640
It depends on what you build around

181
00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:07.120
it.

182
00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.700
Looking at systems in September 2026:

183
00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.220
Codex with agents and evaluations,

184
00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.480
Gemini's agent platform with long-term memory,

185
00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.620
and LangGraph with a human in the

186
00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.770
loop are cultivated from the start.

187
00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.450
Claude Code and

188
00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:23.600
n8n with agents can become cultivated if

189
00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.600
you build an evaluation cycle.

190
00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:29.020
ChatGPT and Gemini with memory are partially

191
00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:29.760
cultivated.

192
00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.090
And API

193
00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:32.500
prompt-and-response, simple RAG,

194
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.640
or a fixed workflow aren't

195
00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:35.380
cultivated.

196
00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.280
Here's a common point of confusion.

197
00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:40.200
Memory alone doesn't make an AI cultivated.

198
00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.620
Here's the difference.

199
00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.160
First case: the agent talks with you

200
00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.480
and saves that you prefer short answers.

201
00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.020
That's personalization.

202
00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.040
It's useful, but it doesn't improve the

203
00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:50.840
process.

204
00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:53.320
Second case: the agent performs a task

205
00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.240
and fails.

206
00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:56.120
The system measures the failure,

207
00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.160
identifies

208
00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.560
the cause, changes the context,

209
00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:00.900
skill, or rule,

210
00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.360
tests again, compares the result,

211
00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.220
and only then keeps the improvement.

212
00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.360
That's cultivation.

213
00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.400
The difference is that in the second

214
00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.680
case, there's evaluation and comparison,

215
00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.040
and the correction goes into the environment

216
00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.720
instead of getting lost in the conversation.

217
00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.460
Let's look at Claude Code as an

218
00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:17.960
example.

219
00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.160
It has the pieces:

220
00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:21.360
subagents, hooks, MCP,

221
00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.980
tools, context, and automation.

222
00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.040
But having the pieces isn't the same

223
00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.500
as having the cycle.

224
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:28.780
If the workflow is:

225
00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.160
create a landing page,

226
00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.200
it delivers, and that's it,

227
00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.460
that's execution.

228
00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.620
Now, if the workflow is:

229
00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.120
Claude creates it,

230
00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.160
tests run, another agent evaluates it,

231
00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.640
errors are recorded,

232
00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.060
Claude gets the feedback,

233
00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.100
corrects it, tests again,

234
00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:47.769
and approved work goes into CLAUDE dot

235
00:06:47.769 --> 00:06:48.820
M D, a skill,

236
00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:51.320
or memory, then you have cultivation.

237
00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:52.840
The tool is the same.

238
00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:55.320
What changed is the system you built

239
00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:56.120
around it.

240
00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:58.360
For teaching and figuring out where you

241
00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:00.060
are, use four levels.

242
00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.480
Level one: executor AI.

243
00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.460
Prompt, response, done.

244
00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:06.640
No memory, no evaluation.

245
00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:09.160
Level two: contextual AI.

246
00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.320
Prompt, context or memory,

247
00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.140
response.

248
00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.760
It personalizes, but it still doesn't have

249
00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.300
an improvement cycle.

250
00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:17.980
Level three: agent.

251
00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:19.120
It gets a goal,

252
00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:20.660
reasons, uses tools,

253
00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:21.960
and takes action.

254
00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.260
For example, it changes the repository,

255
00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:25.180
runs the terminal,

256
00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:26.960
and runs tests.

257
00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:30.520
It's autonomous, but it can repeat the

258
00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:32.820
same mistake a thousand times.

259
00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:34.020
Level

260
00:07:34.233 --> 00:07:37.060
four: IA Cultivada.

261
00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:38.820
Goal, execution,

262
00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:40.680
result, evaluation,

263
00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:43.620
feedback, and what it learned becomes memory,

264
00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:44.980
a skill, context,

265
00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.660
or a rule before the next run.

266
00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:50.180
This is the most important distinction in

267
00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:50.760
the video.

268
00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:52.860
An agent isn't automatically

269
00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.180
IA Cultivada.

270
00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.520
An agent can work nonstop and repeat

271
00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.580
the same mistake thousands of times,

272
00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.060
always with the same confidence.

273
00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:03.100
The leap happens when you add memory,

274
00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:04.300
evaluation,

275
00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:05.860
feedback,

276
00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.060
observability,

277
00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:09.800
clear criteria, correction mechanisms,

278
00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:10.840
and

279
00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.900
the ability to modify the environment.

280
00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:14.580
Remember the formula:

281
00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.020
execution, plus evaluation,

282
00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:21.200
plus feedback, plus adaptation equals cultivation.

283
00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.360
Remove any one of those parts,

284
00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:25.180
and you're back to just an agent,

285
00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:27.400
working hard and learning nothing.

286
00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.140
What does this look like day to

287
00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:29.300
day?

288
00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.480
Three rules.

289
00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.300
First: evaluation produces entries,

290
00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:35.000
not impressions.

291
00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.940
One line per failure in a log:

292
00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:39.580
date, what broke,

293
00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:40.940
the smallest possible correction,

294
00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:43.180
and whether it was an instruction or

295
00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.420
infrastructure problem.

296
